msgid ""
"(B<rateest1> minus B<rateest-pps1>) I<operator> (B<rateest2> minus B<rateest-"
"pps2>)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-delta>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"For each estimator (either absolute or relative mode), calculate the "
"difference between the estimator-determined flow rate and the static value "
"chosen with the BPS/PPS options. If the flow rate is higher than the "
"specified BPS/PPS, 0 will be used instead of a negative value. In other "
"words, \"max(0, rateest#_rate - rateest#_bps)\" is used."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rateest-lt>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match if rate is less than given rate/estimator."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rateest-gt>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match if rate is greater than given rate/estimator."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rateest-eq>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match if rate is equal to given rate/estimator."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"In the so-called \"absolute mode\", only one rate estimator is used and "
"compared against a static value, while in \"relative mode\", two rate "
"estimators are compared against another."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Name of the one rate estimator for absolute mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest1> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest2> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The names of the two rate estimators for relative mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-bps> [I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-pps> [I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-bps1> [I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-bps2> [I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-pps1> [I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-pps2> [I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"Compare the estimator(s) by bytes or packets per second, and compare against "
"the chosen value. See the above bullet list for which option is to be used "
"in which case. A unit suffix may be used - available ones are: bit, "
"[kmgt]bit, [KMGT]ibit, Bps, [KMGT]Bps, [KMGT]iBps."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Example: This is what can be used to route outgoing data connections from an "
"FTP server over two lines based on the available bandwidth at the time the "
"data connection was started:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "# Estimate outgoing rates"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -t mangle -A POSTROUTING -o eth0 -j RATEEST --rateest-name eth0 --"
"rateest-interval 250ms --rateest-ewma 0.5s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -t mangle -A POSTROUTING -o ppp0 -j RATEEST --rateest-name ppp0 --"
"rateest-interval 250ms --rateest-ewma 0.5s"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "# Mark based on available bandwidth"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -t mangle -A balance -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -m helper --helper "
"ftp -m rateest --rateest-delta --rateest1 eth0 --rateest-bps1 2.5mbit --"
"rateest-gt --rateest2 ppp0 --rateest-bps2 2mbit -j CONNMARK --set-mark 1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -t mangle -A balance -m conntrack --ctstate NEW -m helper --helper "
"ftp -m rateest --rateest-delta --rateest1 ppp0 --rateest-bps1 2mbit --"
"rateest-gt --rateest2 eth0 --rateest-bps2 2.5mbit -j CONNMARK --set-mark 2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -t mangle -A balance -j CONNMARK --restore-mark"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "realm (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This matches the routing realm.  Routing realms are used in complex routing "
"setups involving dynamic routing protocols like BGP."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--realm> I<value>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Matches a given realm number (and optionally mask). If not a number, value "
"can be a named realm from /etc/iproute2/rt_realms (mask can not be used in "
"that case).  Both value and mask are four byte unsigned integers and may be "
"specified in decimal, hex (by prefixing with \"0x\") or octal (if a leading "
"zero is given)."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "recent"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Allows you to dynamically create a list of IP addresses and then match "
"against that list in a few different ways."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"For example, you can create a \"badguy\" list out of people attempting to "
"connect to port 139 on your firewall and then DROP all future packets from "
"them without considering them."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"B<--set>, B<--rcheck>, B<--update> and B<--remove> are mutually exclusive."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--name> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Specify the list to use for the commands. If no name is given then "
"B<DEFAULT> will be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--set>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This will add the source address of the packet to the list. If the source "
"address is already in the list, this will update the existing entry. This "
"will always return success (or failure if B<!> is passed in)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rsource>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Match/save the source address of each packet in the recent list table. This "
"is the default."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rdest>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Match/save the destination address of each packet in the recent list table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--mask> I<netmask>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Netmask that will be applied to this recent list."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rcheck>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Check if the source address of the packet is currently in the list."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--update>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Like B<--rcheck>, except it will update the \"last seen\" timestamp if it "
"matches."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--remove>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Check if the source address of the packet is currently in the list and if so "
"that address will be removed from the list and the rule will return true. If "
"the address is not found, false is returned."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--seconds> I<seconds>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This option must be used in conjunction with one of B<--rcheck> or B<--"
"update>. When used, this will narrow the match to only happen when the "
"address is in the list and was seen within the last given number of seconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--reap>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This option can only be used in conjunction with B<--seconds>.  When used, "
"this will cause entries older than the last given number of seconds to be "
"purged."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hitcount> I<hits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"This option must be used in conjunction with one of B<--rcheck> or B<--"
"update>. When used, this will narrow the match to only happen when the "
"address is in the list and packets had been received greater than or equal "
"to the given value. This option may be used along with B<--seconds> to "
"create an even narrower match requiring a certain number of hits within a "
"specific time frame. The maximum value for the hitcount parameter is given "
"by the \"ip_pkt_list_tot\" parameter of the xt_recent kernel module. "
"Exceeding this value on the command line will cause the rule to be rejected."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rttl>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This option may only be used in conjunction with one of B<--rcheck> or B<--"
"update>. When used, this will narrow the match to only happen when the "
"address is in the list and the TTL of the current packet matches that of the "
"packet which hit the B<--set> rule. This may be useful if you have problems "
"with people faking their source address in order to DoS you via this module "
"by disallowing others access to your site by sending bogus packets to you."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -A FORWARD -m recent --name badguy --rcheck --seconds 60 -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -A FORWARD -p tcp -i eth0 --dport 139 -m recent --name badguy --set "
"-j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"B</proc/net/xt_recent/*> are the current lists of addresses and information "
"about each entry of each list."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Each file in B</proc/net/xt_recent/> can be read from to see the current "
"list or written two using the following commands to modify the list:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<echo +>I<addr>B< E<gt>/proc/net/xt_recent/DEFAULT>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "to add I<addr> to the DEFAULT list"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<echo ->I<addr>B< E<gt>/proc/net/xt_recent/DEFAULT>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "to remove I<addr> from the DEFAULT list"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<echo / E<gt>/proc/net/xt_recent/DEFAULT>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "to flush the DEFAULT list (remove all entries)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The module itself accepts parameters, defaults shown:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ip_list_tot>=I<100>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Number of addresses remembered per table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ip_pkt_list_tot>=I<20>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid "Number of packets per address remembered."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ip_list_hash_size>=I<0>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"Hash table size. 0 means to calculate it based on ip_list_tot, default: 512."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ip_list_perms>=I<0644>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Permissions for /proc/net/xt_recent/* files."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ip_list_uid>=I<0>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Numerical UID for ownership of /proc/net/xt_recent/* files."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<ip_list_gid>=I<0>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Numerical GID for ownership of /proc/net/xt_recent/* files."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "rpfilter"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Performs a reverse path filter test on a packet.  If a reply to the packet "
"would be sent via the same interface that the packet arrived on, the packet "
"will match.  Note that, unlike the in-kernel rp_filter, packets protected by "
"IPSec are not treated specially.  Combine this match with the policy match "
"if you want this.  Also, packets arriving via the loopback interface are "
"always permitted.  This match can only be used in the PREROUTING chain of "
"the raw or mangle table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--loose>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Used to specify that the reverse path filter test should match even if the "
"selected output device is not the expected one."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--validmark>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Also use the packets' nfmark value when performing the reverse path route "
"lookup."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--accept-local>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This will permit packets arriving from the network with a source address "
"that is also assigned to the local machine."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--invert>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This will invert the sense of the match.  Instead of matching packets that "
"passed the reverse path filter test, match those that have failed it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Example to log and drop packets failing the reverse path filter test:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -t raw -N RPFILTER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -t raw -A RPFILTER -m rpfilter -j RETURN"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -t raw -A RPFILTER -m limit --limit 10/minute -j NFLOG --nflog-"
"prefix \"rpfilter drop\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -t raw -A RPFILTER -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -t raw -A PREROUTING -j RPFILTER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Example to drop failed packets, without logging:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -t raw -A RPFILTER -m rpfilter --invert -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "rt (IPv6-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match on IPv6 routing header"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rt-type> I<type>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match the type (numeric)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rt-segsleft> I<num>[B<:>I<num>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match the `segments left' field (range)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--rt-len> I<length>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match the length of this header."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rt-0-res>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match the reserved field, too (type=0)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rt-0-addrs> I<addr>[B<,>I<addr>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match type=0 addresses (list)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rt-0-not-strict>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "List of type=0 addresses is not a strict list."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "sctp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "This module matches Stream Control Transmission Protocol headers."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--chunk-types> {B<all>|B<any>|B<only>} I<chunktype>[B<:>I<flags>] [...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The flag letter in upper case indicates that the flag is to match if set, in "
"the lower case indicates to match if unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match types:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "all"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match if all given chunk types are present and flags match."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "any"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match if any of the given chunk types is present with given flags."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "only"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Match if only the given chunk types are present with given flags and none "
"are missing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Chunk types: DATA INIT INIT_ACK SACK HEARTBEAT HEARTBEAT_ACK ABORT SHUTDOWN "
"SHUTDOWN_ACK ERROR COOKIE_ECHO COOKIE_ACK ECN_ECNE ECN_CWR SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE "
"I_DATA RE_CONFIG PAD ASCONF ASCONF_ACK FORWARD_TSN I_FORWARD_TSN"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "chunk type available flags"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "DATA I U B E i u b e"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "I_DATA I U B E i u b e"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "ABORT T t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "SHUTDOWN_COMPLETE T t"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "(lowercase means flag should be \"off\", uppercase means \"on\")"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -A INPUT -p sctp --dport 80 -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -A INPUT -p sctp --chunk-types any DATA,INIT -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -A INPUT -p sctp --chunk-types any DATA:Be -j ACCEPT"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "set"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "This module matches IP sets which can be defined by ipset(8)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--match-set> I<setname> I<flag>[B<,>I<flag>]..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"where flags are the comma separated list of B<src> and/or B<dst> "
"specifications and there can be no more than six of them. Hence the command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid " iptables -A FORWARD -m set --match-set test src,dst\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"will match packets, for which (if the set type is ipportmap) the source "
"address and destination port pair can be found in the specified set. If the "
"set type of the specified set is single dimension (for example ipmap), then "
"the command will match packets for which the source address can be found in "
"the specified set."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--return-nomatch>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the B<--return-nomatch> option is specified and the set type supports the "
"B<nomatch> flag, then the matching is reversed: a match with an element "
"flagged with B<nomatch> returns B<true>, while a match with a plain element "
"returns B<false>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<!> B<--update-counters>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the B<--update-counters> flag is negated, then the packet and byte "
"counters of the matching element in the set won't be updated. Default the "
"packet and byte counters are updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<!> B<--update-subcounters>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the B<--update-subcounters> flag is negated, then the packet and byte "
"counters of the matching element in the member set of a list type of set "
"won't be updated. Default the packet and byte counters are updated."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--packets-eq> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet is matched an element in the set, match only if the packet "
"counter of the element matches the given value too."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--packets-lt> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet is matched an element in the set, match only if the packet "
"counter of the element is less than the given value as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--packets-gt> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet is matched an element in the set, match only if the packet "
"counter of the element is greater than the given value as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--bytes-eq> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet is matched an element in the set, match only if the byte "
"counter of the element matches the given value too."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--bytes-lt> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet is matched an element in the set, match only if the byte "
"counter of the element is less than the given value as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--bytes-gt> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet is matched an element in the set, match only if the byte "
"counter of the element is greater than the given value as well."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The packet and byte counters related options and flags are ignored when the "
"set was defined without counter support."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The option B<--match-set> can be replaced by B<--set> if that does not clash "
"with an option of other extensions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Use of -m set requires that ipset kernel support is provided, which, for "
"standard kernels, is the case since Linux 2.6.39."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "socket"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This matches if an open TCP/UDP socket can be found by doing a socket lookup "
"on the packet. It matches if there is an established or non-zero bound "
"listening socket (possibly with a non-local address). The lookup is "
"performed using the B<packet> tuple of TCP/UDP packets, or the original TCP/"
"UDP header B<embedded> in an ICMP/ICPMv6 error packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--transparent>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Ignore non-transparent sockets."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--nowildcard>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Do not ignore sockets bound to 'any' address.  The socket match won't accept "
"zero-bound listeners by default, since then local services could intercept "
"traffic that would otherwise be forwarded.  This option therefore has "
"security implications when used to match traffic being forwarded to redirect "
"such packets to local machine with policy routing.  When using the socket "
"match to implement fully transparent proxies bound to non-local addresses it "
"is recommended to use the --transparent option instead."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Example (assuming packets with mark 1 are delivered locally):"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-t mangle -A PREROUTING -m socket --transparent -j MARK --set-mark 1"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--restore-skmark>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the packet mark to the matching socket's mark. Can be combined with the "
"B<--transparent> and B<--nowildcard> options to restrict the sockets to be "
"matched when restoring the packet mark."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Example: An application opens 2 transparent (B<IP_TRANSPARENT>) sockets and "
"sets a mark on them with B<SO_MARK> socket option. We can filter matching "
"packets:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"-t mangle -I PREROUTING -m socket --transparent --restore-skmark -j action"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-t mangle -A action -m mark --mark 10 -j action2"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-t mangle -A action -m mark --mark 11 -j action3"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "state"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The \"state\" extension is a subset of the \"conntrack\" module.  \"state\" "
"allows access to the connection tracking state for this packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--state> I<state>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Where state is a comma separated list of the connection states to match. "
"Only a subset of the states unterstood by \"conntrack\" are recognized: "
"B<INVALID>, B<ESTABLISHED>, B<NEW>, B<RELATED> or B<UNTRACKED>. For their "
"description, see the \"conntrack\" heading in this manpage."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "statistic"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module matches packets based on some statistic condition.  It supports "
"two distinct modes settable with the B<--mode> option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Supported options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--mode> I<mode>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the matching mode of the matching rule, supported modes are B<random> "
"and B<nth.>"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--probability> I<p>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the probability for a packet to be randomly matched. It only works with "
"the B<random> mode. I<p> must be within 0.0 and 1.0. The supported "
"granularity is in 1/2147483648th increments."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--every> I<n>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Match one packet every nth packet. It works only with the B<nth> mode (see "
"also the B<--packet> option)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--packet> I<p>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the initial counter value (0 E<lt>= p E<lt>= n-1, default 0) for the "
"B<nth> mode."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "string"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module matches a given string by using some pattern matching strategy. "
"It requires a linux kernel E<gt>= 2.6.14."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--algo> {B<bm>|B<kmp>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Select the pattern matching strategy. (bm = Boyer-Moore, kmp = Knuth-Pratt-"
"Morris)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--from> I<offset>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the offset from which it starts looking for any matching. If not passed, "
"default is 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--to> I<offset>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"Set the offset up to which should be scanned. That is, byte I<offset>-1 "
"(counting from 0) is the last one that is scanned.  If not passed, default "
"is the packet size."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--string> I<pattern>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Matches the given pattern."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--hex-string> I<pattern>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Matches the given pattern in hex notation."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--icase>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Ignore case when searching."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "# The string pattern can be used for simple text characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 80 -m string --algo bm --string 'GET /"
"index.html' -j LOG"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"# The hex string pattern can be used for non-printable characters, like |0D "
"0A| or |0D0A|."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -p udp --dport 53 -m string --algo bm --from 40 --to 57 --hex-"
"string '|03|www|09|netfilter|03|org|00|'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Note: Since Boyer-Moore (BM) performs searches for matches from right to "
"left and the kernel may store a packet in multiple discontiguous blocks, "
"it's possible that a match could be spread over multiple blocks, in which "
"case this algorithm won't find it."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If you wish to ensure that such thing won't ever happen, use the Knuth-Pratt-"
"Morris (KMP) algorithm instead.  In conclusion, choose the proper string "
"search algorithm depending on your use-case."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"For example, if you're using the module for filtering, NIDS or any similar "
"security-focused purpose, then choose KMP. On the other hand, if you really "
"care about performance \\(em for example, you're classifying packets to "
"apply Quality of Service (QoS) policies \\(em and you don't mind about "
"missing possible matches spread over multiple fragments, then choose BM."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "tcp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"These extensions can be used if `--protocol tcp' is specified. It provides "
"the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Source port or port range specification. This can either be a service name "
"or a port number. An inclusive range can also be specified, using the format "
"I<first>B<:>I<last>.  If the first port is omitted, \"0\" is assumed; if the "
"last is omitted, \"65535\" is assumed.  The flag B<--sport> is a convenient "
"alias for this option."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Destination port or port range specification.  The flag B<--dport> is a "
"convenient alias for this option."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--tcp-flags> I<mask> I<comp>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Match when the TCP flags are as specified.  The first argument I<mask> is "
"the flags which we should examine, written as a comma-separated list, and "
"the second argument I<comp> is a comma-separated list of flags which must be "
"set.  Flags are: B<SYN ACK FIN RST URG PSH ALL NONE>.  Hence the command"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid " iptables -A FORWARD -p tcp --tcp-flags SYN,ACK,FIN,RST SYN\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"will only match packets with the SYN flag set, and the ACK, FIN and RST "
"flags unset."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--syn>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only match TCP packets with the SYN bit set and the ACK,RST and FIN bits "
"cleared.  Such packets are used to request TCP connection initiation; for "
"example, blocking such packets coming in an interface will prevent incoming "
"TCP connections, but outgoing TCP connections will be unaffected.  It is "
"equivalent to B<--tcp-flags SYN,RST,ACK,FIN SYN>.  If the \"!\" flag "
"precedes the \"--syn\", the sense of the option is inverted."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--tcp-option> I<number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Match if TCP option set."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "tcpmss"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This matches the TCP MSS (maximum segment size) field of the TCP header.  "
"You can only use this on TCP SYN or SYN/ACK packets, since the MSS is only "
"negotiated during the TCP handshake at connection startup time."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--mss> I<value>[B<:>I<value>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Match a given TCP MSS value or range. If a range is given, the second "
"I<value> must be greater than or equal to the first I<value>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "time"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This matches if the packet arrival time/date is within a given range. All "
"options are optional, but are ANDed when specified. All times are "
"interpreted as UTC by default."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--datestart> I<YYYY>[B<->I<MM>[B<->I<DD>[B<T>I<hh>[B<:>I<mm>[B<:>I<ss>]]]]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--datestop> I<YYYY>[B<->I<MM>[B<->I<DD>[B<T>I<hh>[B<:>I<mm>[B<:>I<ss>]]]]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only match during the given time, which must be in ISO 8601 \"T\" notation.  "
"The possible time range is 1970-01-01T00:00:00 to 2038-01-19T04:17:07."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If --datestart or --datestop are not specified, it will default to "
"1970-01-01 and 2038-01-19, respectively."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--timestart> I<hh>B<:>I<mm>[B<:>I<ss>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--timestop> I<hh>B<:>I<mm>[B<:>I<ss>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only match during the given daytime. The possible time range is 00:00:00 to "
"23:59:59. Leading zeroes are allowed (e.g. \"06:03\") and correctly "
"interpreted as base-10."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--monthdays> I<day>[B<,>I<day>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only match on the given days of the month. Possible values are B<1> to "
"B<31>. Note that specifying B<31> will of course not match on months which "
"do not have a 31st day; the same goes for 28- or 29-day February."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--weekdays> I<day>[B<,>I<day>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only match on the given weekdays. Possible values are B<Mon>, B<Tue>, "
"B<Wed>, B<Thu>, B<Fri>, B<Sat>, B<Sun>, or values from B<1> to B<7>, "
"respectively. You may also use two-character variants (B<Mo>, B<Tu>, etc.)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--contiguous>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"When B<--timestop> is smaller than B<--timestart> value, match this as a "
"single time period instead distinct intervals.  See EXAMPLES."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--kerneltz>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Use the kernel timezone instead of UTC to determine whether a packet meets "
"the time regulations."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"About kernel timezones: Linux keeps the system time in UTC, and always does "
"so.  On boot, system time is initialized from a referential time source. "
"Where this time source has no timezone information, such as the x86 CMOS "
"RTC, UTC will be assumed. If the time source is however not in UTC, "
"userspace should provide the correct system time and timezone to the kernel "
"once it has the information."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Local time is a feature on top of the (timezone independent) system time. "
"Each process has its own idea of local time, specified via the TZ "
"environment variable. The kernel also has its own timezone offset variable. "
"The TZ userspace environment variable specifies how the UTC-based system "
"time is displayed, e.g. when you run date(1), or what you see on your "
"desktop clock.  The TZ string may resolve to different offsets at different "
"dates, which is what enables the automatic time-jumping in userspace. when "
"DST changes. The kernel's timezone offset variable is used when it has to "
"convert between non-UTC sources, such as FAT filesystems, to UTC (since the "
"latter is what the rest of the system uses)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"The caveat with the kernel timezone is that Linux distributions may ignore "
"to set the kernel timezone, and instead only set the system time. Even if a "
"particular distribution does set the timezone at boot, it is usually does "
"not keep the kernel timezone offset - which is what changes on DST - up to "
"date.  ntpd will not touch the kernel timezone, so running it will not "
"resolve the issue. As such, one may encounter a timezone that is always "
"+0000, or one that is wrong half of the time of the year. As such, B<using --"
"kerneltz is highly discouraged.>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "EXAMPLES. To match on weekends, use:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-m time --weekdays Sa,Su"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Or, to match (once) on a national holiday block:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-m time --datestart 2007-12-24 --datestop 2007-12-27"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Since the stop time is actually inclusive, you would need the following stop "
"time to not match the first second of the new day:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-m time --datestart 2007-01-01T17:00 --datestop 2007-01-01T23:59:59"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "During lunch hour:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-m time --timestart 12:30 --timestop 13:30"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The fourth Friday in the month:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-m time --weekdays Fr --monthdays 22,23,24,25,26,27,28"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"(Note that this exploits a certain mathematical property. It is not possible "
"to say \"fourth Thursday OR fourth Friday\" in one rule. It is possible with "
"multiple rules, though.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Matching across days might not do what is expected.  For instance,"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"-m time --weekdays Mo --timestart 23:00 --timestop 01:00 Will match Monday, "
"for one hour from midnight to 1 a.m., and then again for another hour from "
"23:00 onwards.  If this is unwanted, e.g. if you would like 'match for two "
"hours from Montay 23:00 onwards' you need to also specify the --contiguous "
"option in the example above."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "tos"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module matches the 8-bit Type of Service field in the IPv4 header "
"(i.e.  including the \"Precedence\" bits) or the (also 8-bit) Priority field "
"in the IPv6 header."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--tos> I<value>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Matches packets with the given TOS mark value. If a mask is specified, it is "
"logically ANDed with the TOS mark before the comparison."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--tos> I<symbol>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"You can specify a symbolic name when using the tos match for IPv4. The list "
"of recognized TOS names can be obtained by calling iptables with B<-m tos "
"-h>.  Note that this implies a mask of 0x3F, i.e. all but the ECN bits."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "ttl (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "This module matches the time to live field in the IP header."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--ttl-eq> I<ttl>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Matches the given TTL value."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ttl-gt> I<ttl>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Matches if TTL is greater than the given TTL value."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ttl-lt> I<ttl>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Matches if TTL is less than the given TTL value."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "u32"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"U32 tests whether quantities of up to 4 bytes extracted from a packet have "
"specified values. The specification of what to extract is general enough to "
"find data at given offsets from tcp headers or payloads."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "[B<!>] B<--u32> I<tests>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The argument amounts to a program in a small language described below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "tests := location \"=\" value | tests \"&&\" location \"=\" value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "value := range | value \",\" range"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "range := number | number \":\" number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"a single number, I<n>, is interpreted the same as I<n:n>. I<n:m> is "
"interpreted as the range of numbers B<E<gt>=n> and B<E<lt>=m>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "location := number | location operator number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "operator := \"&\" | \"E<lt>E<lt>\" | \"E<gt>E<gt>\" | \"@\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The operators B<&>, B<E<lt>E<lt>>, B<E<gt>E<gt>> and B<&&> mean the same as "
"in C.  The B<=> is really a set membership operator and the value syntax "
"describes a set. The B<@> operator is what allows moving to the next header "
"and is described further below."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"There are currently some artificial implementation limits on the size of the "
"tests:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    *"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "no more than 10 of \"B<=>\" (and 9 \"B<&&>\"s) in the u32 argument"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "no more than 10 ranges (and 9 commas) per value"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "no more than 10 numbers (and 9 operators) per location"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"To describe the meaning of location, imagine the following machine that "
"interprets it. There are three registers:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "A is of type B<char *>, initially the address of the IP header"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "B and C are unsigned 32 bit integers, initially zero"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The instructions are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "B = number;"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"C = (*(A+B)E<lt>E<lt>24) + (*(A+B+1)E<lt>E<lt>16) + (*(A+B+2)E<lt>E<lt>8) + "
"*(A+B+3)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<&number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "C = C & number"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<E<lt>E<lt> number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "C = C E<lt>E<lt> number"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<E<gt>E<gt> number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "C = C E<gt>E<gt> number"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<@number>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "A = A + C; then do the instruction number"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Any access of memory outside [skb-E<gt>data,skb-E<gt>end] causes the match "
"to fail.  Otherwise the result of the computation is the final value of C."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Whitespace is allowed but not required in the tests. However, the characters "
"that do occur there are likely to require shell quoting, so it is a good "
"idea to enclose the arguments in quotes."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "match IP packets with total length E<gt>= 256"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid "The IP header contains a total length field in bytes 2-3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "--u32 \"B<0 & 0xFFFF = 0x100:0xFFFF>\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid "read bytes 0-3"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"AND that with 0xFFFF (giving bytes 2-3), and test whether that is in the "
"range [0x100:0xFFFF]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Example: (more realistic, hence more complicated)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "match ICMP packets with icmp type 0"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "First test that it is an ICMP packet, true iff byte 9 (protocol) = 1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "--u32 \"B<6 & 0xFF = 1 &&> ..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"read bytes 6-9, use B<&> to throw away bytes 6-8 and compare the result to "
"1. Next test that it is not a fragment. (If so, it might be part of such a "
"packet but we cannot always tell.) N.B.: This test is generally needed if "
"you want to match anything beyond the IP header. The last 6 bits of byte 6 "
"and all of byte 7 are 0 iff this is a complete packet (not a fragment). "
"Alternatively, you can allow first fragments by only testing the last 5 bits "
"of byte 6."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "... B<4 & 0x3FFF = 0 &&> ..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Last test: the first byte past the IP header (the type) is 0. This is where "
"we have to use the @syntax. The length of the IP header (IHL) in 32 bit "
"words is stored in the right half of byte 0 of the IP header itself."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "... B<0 E<gt>E<gt> 22 & 0x3C @ 0 E<gt>E<gt> 24 = 0>\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"The first 0 means read bytes 0-3, B<E<gt>E<gt>22> means shift that 22 bits "
"to the right. Shifting 24 bits would give the first byte, so only 22 bits is "
"four times that plus a few more bits. B<&3C> then eliminates the two extra "
"bits on the right and the first four bits of the first byte. For instance, "
"if IHL=5, then the IP header is 20 (4 x 5) bytes long. In this case, bytes "
"0-1 are (in binary) xxxx0101 yyzzzzzz, B<E<gt>E<gt>22> gives the 10 bit "
"value xxxx0101yy and B<&3C> gives 010100. B<@> means to use this number as a "
"new offset into the packet, and read four bytes starting from there. This is "
"the first 4 bytes of the ICMP payload, of which byte 0 is the ICMP type. "
"Therefore, we simply shift the value 24 to the right to throw out all but "
"the first byte and compare the result with 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid "TCP payload bytes 8-12 is any of 1, 2, 5 or 8"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "First we test that the packet is a tcp packet (similar to ICMP)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "--u32 \"B<6 & 0xFF = 6 &&> ..."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Next, test that it is not a fragment (same as above)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "... B<0 E<gt>E<gt> 22 & 0x3C @ 12 E<gt>E<gt> 26 & 0x3C @ 8 = 1,2,5,8>\""
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"B<0E<gt>E<gt>22&3C> as above computes the number of bytes in the IP header. "
"B<@> makes this the new offset into the packet, which is the start of the "
"TCP header. The length of the TCP header (again in 32 bit words) is the left "
"half of byte 12 of the TCP header. The B<12E<gt>E<gt>26&3C> computes this "
"length in bytes (similar to the IP header before). \"@\" makes this the new "
"offset, which is the start of the TCP payload. Finally, 8 reads bytes 8-12 "
"of the payload and B<=> checks whether the result is any of 1, 2, 5 or 8."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "udp"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"These extensions can be used if `--protocol udp' is specified. It provides "
"the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Source port or port range specification.  See the description of the B<--"
"source-port> option of the TCP extension for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Destination port or port range specification.  See the description of the "
"B<--destination-port> option of the TCP extension for details."
msgstr ""

#. type: SH
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TARGET EXTENSIONS"
msgstr ""

#.  @TARGET@
#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables can use extended target modules: the following are included in the "
"standard distribution."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "AUDIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target creates audit records for packets hitting the target.  It can be "
"used to record accepted, dropped, and rejected packets. See auditd(8) for "
"additional details."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--type> {B<accept>|B<drop>|B<reject>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set type of audit record. Starting with linux-4.12, this option has no "
"effect on generated audit messages anymore. It is still accepted by iptables "
"for compatibility reasons, but ignored."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -N AUDIT_DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -A AUDIT_DROP -j AUDIT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -A AUDIT_DROP -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "CHECKSUM"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target selectively works around broken/old applications.  It can only "
"be used in the mangle table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--checksum-fill>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Compute and fill in the checksum in a packet that lacks a checksum.  This is "
"particularly useful, if you need to work around old applications such as "
"dhcp clients, that do not work well with checksum offloads, but don't want "
"to disable checksum offload in your device."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLASSIFY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module allows you to set the skb-E<gt>priority value (and thus classify "
"the packet into a specific CBQ class)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-class> I<major>B<:>I<minor>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the major and minor class value. The values are always interpreted as "
"hexadecimal even if no 0x prefix is given."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "CLUSTERIP (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module allows you to configure a simple cluster of nodes that share a "
"certain IP and MAC address without an explicit load balancer in front of "
"them.  Connections are statically distributed between the nodes in this "
"cluster."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Please note that CLUSTERIP target is considered deprecated in favour of "
"cluster match which is more flexible and not limited to IPv4."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--new>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Create a new ClusterIP.  You always have to set this on the first rule for a "
"given ClusterIP."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hashmode> I<mode>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Specify the hashing mode.  Has to be one of B<sourceip>, B<sourceip-"
"sourceport>, B<sourceip-sourceport-destport>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--clustermac> I<mac>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Specify the ClusterIP MAC address. Has to be a link-layer multicast address"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--total-nodes> I<num>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Number of total nodes within this cluster."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--local-node> I<num>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Local node number within this cluster."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hash-init> I<rnd>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Specify the random seed used for hash initialization."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONNMARK"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module sets the netfilter mark value associated with a connection. The "
"mark is 32 bits wide."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-xmark> I<value>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Zero out the bits given by I<mask> and XOR I<value> into the ctmark."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--save-mark> [B<--nfmask> I<nfmask>] [B<--ctmask> I<ctmask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Copy the packet mark (nfmark) to the connection mark (ctmark) using the "
"given masks. The new nfmark value is determined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid "ctmark = (ctmark & ~ctmask) ^ (nfmark & nfmask)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"i.e. I<ctmask> defines what bits to clear and I<nfmask> what bits of the "
"nfmark to XOR into the ctmark. I<ctmask> and I<nfmask> default to 0xFFFFFFFF."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--restore-mark> [B<--nfmask> I<nfmask>] [B<--ctmask> I<ctmask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Copy the connection mark (ctmark) to the packet mark (nfmark) using the "
"given masks. The new ctmark value is determined as follows:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid "nfmark = (nfmark & ~I<nfmask>) ^ (ctmark & I<ctmask>);"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"i.e. I<nfmask> defines what bits to clear and I<ctmask> what bits of the "
"ctmark to XOR into the nfmark. I<ctmask> and I<nfmask> default to 0xFFFFFFFF."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "B<--restore-mark> is only valid in the B<mangle> table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The following mnemonics are available for B<--set-xmark>:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--and-mark> I<bits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary AND the ctmark with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-xmark 0/"
">I<invbits>, where I<invbits> is the binary negation of I<bits>.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--or-mark> I<bits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary OR the ctmark with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-xmark> I<bits>B</"
">I<bits>.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--xor-mark> I<bits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary XOR the ctmark with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-xmark> I<bits>B</"
"0>.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-mark> I<value>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set the connection mark. If a mask is specified then only those bits set in "
"the mask are modified."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--save-mark> [B<--mask> I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Copy the nfmark to the ctmark. If a mask is specified, only those bits are "
"copied."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--restore-mark> [B<--mask> I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Copy the ctmark to the nfmark. If a mask is specified, only those bits are "
"copied. This is only valid in the B<mangle> table."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "CONNSECMARK"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module copies security markings from packets to connections (if "
"unlabeled), and from connections back to packets (also only if unlabeled).  "
"Typically used in conjunction with SECMARK, it is valid in the B<security> "
"table (for backwards compatibility with older kernels, it is also valid in "
"the B<mangle> table)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--save>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet has a security marking, copy it to the connection if the "
"connection is not marked."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--restore>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"If the packet does not have a security marking, and the connection does, "
"copy the security marking from the connection to the packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "CT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The CT target sets parameters for a packet or its associated connection. The "
"target attaches a \"template\" connection tracking entry to the packet, "
"which is then used by the conntrack core when initializing a new ct entry. "
"This target is thus only valid in the \"raw\" table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--notrack>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Disables connection tracking for this packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--helper> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Use the helper identified by I<name> for the connection. This is more "
"flexible than loading the conntrack helper modules with preset ports."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ctevents> I<event>[B<,>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only generate the specified conntrack events for this connection. Possible "
"event types are: B<new>, B<related>, B<destroy>, B<reply>, B<assured>, "
"B<protoinfo>, B<helper>, B<mark> (this refers to the ctmark, not nfmark), "
"B<natseqinfo>, B<secmark> (ctsecmark)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--expevents> I<event>[B<,>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Only generate the specified expectation events for this connection.  "
"Possible event types are: B<new>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--zone-orig> {I<id>|B<mark>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"For traffic coming from ORIGINAL direction, assign this packet to zone I<id> "
"and only have lookups done in that zone. If B<mark> is used instead of "
"I<id>, the zone is derived from the packet nfmark."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--zone-reply> {I<id>|B<mark>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"For traffic coming from REPLY direction, assign this packet to zone I<id> "
"and only have lookups done in that zone. If B<mark> is used instead of "
"I<id>, the zone is derived from the packet nfmark."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--zone> {I<id>|B<mark>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Assign this packet to zone I<id> and only have lookups done in that zone.  "
"If B<mark> is used instead of I<id>, the zone is derived from the packet "
"nfmark. By default, packets have zone 0. This option applies to both "
"directions."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--timeout> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Use the timeout policy identified by I<name> for the connection. This is "
"provides more flexible timeout policy definition than global timeout values "
"available at /proc/sys/net/netfilter/nf_conntrack_*_timeout_*."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "DNAT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is only valid in the B<nat> table, in the B<PREROUTING> and "
"B<OUTPUT> chains, and user-defined chains which are only called from those "
"chains.  It specifies that the destination address of the packet should be "
"modified (and all future packets in this connection will also be mangled), "
"and rules should cease being examined.  It takes the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--to-destination> [I<ipaddr>[B<->I<ipaddr>]][B<:>I<port>[B<->I<port>[B</>I<baseport>B<]]]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"which can specify a single new destination IP address, an inclusive range of "
"IP addresses. Optionally a port range, if the rule also specifies one of the "
"following protocols: B<tcp>, B<udp>, B<dccp> or B<sctp>.  If no port range "
"is specified, then the destination port will never be modified. If no IP "
"address is specified then only the destination port will be modified.  If "
"B<baseport> is given, the difference of the original destination port and "
"its value is used as offset into the mapping port range. This allows to "
"create shifted portmap ranges and is available since kernel version 4.18.  "
"For a single port or I<baseport>, a service name as listed in B</etc/"
"services> may be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--random>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Randomize source port mapping (kernel E<gt>= 2.6.22)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--persistent>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Gives a client the same source-/destination-address for each connection.  "
"This supersedes the SAME target. Support for persistent mappings is "
"available from 2.6.29-rc2."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "IPv6 support available since Linux kernels E<gt>= 3.7."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "DNPT (IPv6-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Provides stateless destination IPv6-to-IPv6 Network Prefix Translation (as "
"described by RFC 6296)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"You have to use this target in the B<mangle> table, not in the B<nat> table. "
"It takes the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--src-pfx> [I<prefix/>I<length]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Set source prefix that you want to translate and length"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--dst-pfx> [I<prefix/>I<length]>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Set destination prefix that you want to use in the translation and length"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "You have to use the SNPT target to undo the translation. Example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"ip6tables -t mangle -I POSTROUTING -s fd00::/64 \\! -o vboxnet0 -j SNPT --"
"src-pfx fd00::/64 --dst-pfx 2001:e20:2000:40f::/64"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"ip6tables -t mangle -I PREROUTING -i wlan0 -d 2001:e20:2000:40f::/64 -j DNPT "
"--src-pfx 2001:e20:2000:40f::/64 --dst-pfx fd00::/64"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "You may need to enable IPv6 neighbor proxy:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "sysctl -w net.ipv6.conf.all.proxy_ndp=1"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"You also have to use the B<NOTRACK> target to disable connection tracking "
"for translated flows."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "DSCP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target alters the value of the DSCP bits within the TOS header of the "
"IPv4 packet.  As this manipulates a packet, it can only be used in the "
"mangle table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-dscp> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Set the DSCP field to a numerical value (can be decimal or hex)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-dscp-class> I<class>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Set the DSCP field to a DiffServ class."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "ECN (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target selectively works around known ECN blackholes.  It can only be "
"used in the mangle table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ecn-tcp-remove>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Remove all ECN bits from the TCP header.  Of course, it can only be used in "
"conjunction with B<-p tcp>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "HL (IPv6-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is used to modify the Hop Limit field in IPv6 header. The Hop Limit "
"field is similar to what is known as TTL value in IPv4.  Setting or "
"incrementing the Hop Limit field can potentially be very dangerous, so it "
"should be avoided at any cost. This target is only valid in B<mangle> table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"B<Don't ever set or increment the value on packets that leave your local "
"network!>"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hl-set> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Set the Hop Limit to `value'."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hl-dec> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Decrement the Hop Limit `value' times."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hl-inc> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Increment the Hop Limit `value' times."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "HMARK"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Like MARK, i.e. set the fwmark, but the mark is calculated from hashing "
"packet selector at choice. You have also to specify the mark range and, "
"optionally, the offset to start from. ICMP error messages are inspected and "
"used to calculate the hashing."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Existing options are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-tuple> tuple"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Possible tuple members are: B<src> meaning source address (IPv4, IPv6 "
"address), B<dst> meaning destination address (IPv4, IPv6 address), B<sport> "
"meaning source port (TCP, UDP, UDPlite, SCTP, DCCP), B<dport> meaning "
"destination port (TCP, UDP, UDPlite, SCTP, DCCP), B<spi> meaning Security "
"Parameter Index (AH, ESP), and B<ct> meaning the usage of the conntrack "
"tuple instead of the packet selectors."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-mod> I<value (must be E<gt> 0)>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Modulus for hash calculation (to limit the range of possible marks)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-offset> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Offset to start marks from."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "For advanced usage, instead of using --hmark-tuple, you can specify custom"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "prefixes and masks:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-src-prefix> I<cidr>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The source address mask in CIDR notation."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-dst-prefix> I<cidr>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The destination address mask in CIDR notation."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-sport-mask> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "A 16 bit source port mask in hexadecimal."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-dport-mask> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "A 16 bit destination port mask in hexadecimal."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-spi-mask> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "A 32 bit field with spi mask."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-proto-mask> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "An 8 bit field with layer 4 protocol number."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--hmark-rnd> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "A 32 bit random custom value to feed hash calculation."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "I<Examples:>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"iptables -t mangle -A PREROUTING -m conntrack --ctstate NEW\n"
" -j HMARK --hmark-tuple ct,src,dst,proto --hmark-offset 10000\n"
"--hmark-mod 10 --hmark-rnd 0xfeedcafe\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -t mangle -A PREROUTING -j HMARK --hmark-offset 10000 --hmark-tuple "
"src,dst,proto --hmark-mod 10 --hmark-rnd 0xdeafbeef"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "IDLETIMER"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target can be used to identify when interfaces have been idle for a "
"certain period of time.  Timers are identified by labels and are created "
"when a rule is set with a new label.  The rules also take a timeout value "
"(in seconds) as an option.  If more than one rule uses the same timer label, "
"the timer will be restarted whenever any of the rules get a hit.  One entry "
"for each timer is created in sysfs.  This attribute contains the timer "
"remaining for the timer to expire.  The attributes are located under the "
"xt_idletimer class:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "/sys/class/xt_idletimer/timers/E<lt>labelE<gt>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"When the timer expires, the target module sends a sysfs notification to the "
"userspace, which can then decide what to do (eg. disconnect to save power)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--timeout> I<amount>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "This is the time in seconds that will trigger the notification."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--label> I<string>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is a unique identifier for the timer.  The maximum length for the label "
"string is 27 characters."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "LED"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This creates an LED-trigger that can then be attached to system indicator "
"lights, to blink or illuminate them when certain packets pass through the "
"system. One example might be to light up an LED for a few minutes every time "
"an SSH connection is made to the local machine. The following options "
"control the trigger behavior:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--led-trigger-id> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is the name given to the LED trigger. The actual name of the trigger "
"will be prefixed with \"netfilter-\"."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--led-delay> I<ms>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This indicates how long (in milliseconds) the LED should be left illuminated "
"when a packet arrives before being switched off again. The default is 0 "
"(blink as fast as possible.) The special value I<inf> can be given to leave "
"the LED on permanently once activated. (In this case the trigger will need "
"to be manually detached and reattached to the LED device to switch it off "
"again.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--led-always-blink>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Always make the LED blink on packet arrival, even if the LED is already on.  "
"This allows notification of new packets even with long delay values (which "
"otherwise would result in a silent prolonging of the delay time.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "Create an LED trigger for incoming SSH traffic:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "iptables -A INPUT -p tcp --dport 22 -j LED --led-trigger-id ssh"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "Then attach the new trigger to an LED:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "echo netfilter-ssh E<gt>/sys/class/leds/I<ledname>/trigger"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "LOG"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Turn on kernel logging of matching packets.  When this option is set for a "
"rule, the Linux kernel will print some information on all matching packets "
"(like most IP/IPv6 header fields) via the kernel log (where it can be read "
"with I<dmesg(1)> or read in the syslog)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is a \"non-terminating target\", i.e. rule traversal continues at the "
"next rule.  So if you want to LOG the packets you refuse, use two separate "
"rules with the same matching criteria, first using target LOG then DROP (or "
"REJECT)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-level> I<level>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Level of logging, which can be (system-specific) numeric or a mnemonic.  "
"Possible values are (in decreasing order of priority): B<emerg>, B<alert>, "
"B<crit>, B<error>, B<warning>, B<notice>, B<info> or B<debug>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-prefix> I<prefix>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Prefix log messages with the specified prefix; up to 29 letters long, and "
"useful for distinguishing messages in the logs."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-tcp-sequence>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Log TCP sequence numbers. This is a security risk if the log is readable by "
"users."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-tcp-options>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Log options from the TCP packet header."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-ip-options>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Log options from the IP/IPv6 packet header."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-uid>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Log the userid of the process which generated the packet."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--log-macdecode>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Log MAC addresses and protocol."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "MARK"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is used to set the Netfilter mark value associated with the "
"packet.  It can, for example, be used in conjunction with routing based on "
"fwmark (needs iproute2). If you plan on doing so, note that the mark needs "
"to be set in either the PREROUTING or the OUTPUT chain of the mangle table "
"to affect routing.  The mark field is 32 bits wide."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Zeroes out the bits given by I<mask> and XORs I<value> into the packet mark "
"(\"nfmark\"). If I<mask> is omitted, 0xFFFFFFFF is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Zeroes out the bits given by I<mask> and ORs I<value> into the packet mark. "
"If I<mask> is omitted, 0xFFFFFFFF is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "The following mnemonics are available:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary AND the nfmark with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-xmark 0/"
">I<invbits>, where I<invbits> is the binary negation of I<bits>.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary OR the nfmark with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-xmark> I<bits>B</"
">I<bits>.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary XOR the nfmark with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-xmark> I<bits>B</"
"0>.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "MASQUERADE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is only valid in the B<nat> table, in the B<POSTROUTING> chain.  "
"It should only be used with dynamically assigned IP (dialup)  connections: "
"if you have a static IP address, you should use the SNAT target.  "
"Masquerading is equivalent to specifying a mapping to the IP address of the "
"interface the packet is going out, but also has the effect that connections "
"are I<forgotten> when the interface goes down.  This is the correct behavior "
"when the next dialup is unlikely to have the same interface address (and "
"hence any established connections are lost anyway)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--to-ports> I<port>[B<->I<port>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"This specifies a range of source ports to use, overriding the default "
"B<SNAT> source port-selection heuristics (see above).  This is only valid if "
"the rule also specifies one of the following protocols: B<tcp>, B<udp>, "
"B<dccp> or B<sctp>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Randomize source port mapping (kernel E<gt>= 2.6.21).  Since kernel 5.0, B<--"
"random> is identical to B<--random-fully>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--random-fully>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Fully randomize source port mapping (kernel E<gt>= 3.13)."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "NETMAP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target allows you to statically map a whole network of addresses onto "
"another network of addresses.  It can only be used from rules in the B<nat> "
"table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--to> I<address>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Network address to map to.  The resulting address will be constructed in the "
"following way: All 'one' bits in the mask are filled in from the new "
"`address'.  All bits that are zero in the mask are filled in from the "
"original address."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "NFLOG"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target provides logging of matching packets. When this target is set "
"for a rule, the Linux kernel will pass the packet to the loaded logging "
"backend to log the packet. This is usually used in combination with "
"nfnetlink_log as logging backend, which will multicast the packet through a "
"I<netlink> socket to the specified multicast group. One or more userspace "
"processes may subscribe to the group to receive the packets. Like LOG, this "
"is a non-terminating target, i.e. rule traversal continues at the next rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--nflog-group> I<nlgroup>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"The netlink group (0 - 2^16-1) to which packets are (only applicable for "
"nfnetlink_log). The default value is 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--nflog-prefix> I<prefix>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"A prefix string to include in the log message, up to 64 characters long, "
"useful for distinguishing messages in the logs."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--nflog-range> I<size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "This option has never worked, use --nflog-size instead"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--nflog-size> I<size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The number of bytes to be copied to userspace (only applicable for "
"nfnetlink_log). nfnetlink_log instances may specify their own range, this "
"option overrides it."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--nflog-threshold> I<size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Number of packets to queue inside the kernel before sending them to "
"userspace (only applicable for nfnetlink_log). Higher values result in less "
"overhead per packet, but increase delay until the packets reach userspace. "
"The default value is 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "NFQUEUE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target passes the packet to userspace using the B<nfnetlink_queue> "
"handler.  The packet is put into the queue identified by its 16-bit queue "
"number.  Userspace can inspect and modify the packet if desired. Userspace "
"must then drop or reinject the packet into the kernel.  Please see "
"libnetfilter_queue for details.  B<nfnetlink_queue> was added in Linux "
"2.6.14. The B<queue-balance> option was added in Linux 2.6.31, B<queue-"
"bypass> in 2.6.39."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--queue-num> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This specifies the QUEUE number to use. Valid queue numbers are 0 to 65535. "
"The default value is 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--queue-balance> I<value>B<:>I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This specifies a range of queues to use. Packets are then balanced across "
"the given queues.  This is useful for multicore systems: start multiple "
"instances of the userspace program on queues x, x+1, .. x+n and use \"--"
"queue-balance I<x>B<:>I<x+n>\".  Packets belonging to the same connection "
"are put into the same nfqueue.  Due to implementation details, a lower range "
"value of 0 limits the higher range value to 65534, i.e. one can only balance "
"between at most 65535 queues."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--queue-bypass>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"By default, if no userspace program is listening on an NFQUEUE, then all "
"packets that are to be queued are dropped.  When this option is used, the "
"NFQUEUE rule behaves like ACCEPT instead, and the packet will move on to the "
"next table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--queue-cpu-fanout>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Available starting Linux kernel 3.10. When used together with B<--queue-"
"balance> this will use the CPU ID as an index to map packets to the queues. "
"The idea is that you can improve performance if there's a queue per CPU. "
"This requires B<--queue-balance> to be specified."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "NOTRACK"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This extension disables connection tracking for all packets matching that "
"rule.  It is equivalent with -j CT --notrack. Like CT, NOTRACK can only be "
"used in the B<raw> table."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "RATEEST"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The RATEEST target collects statistics, performs rate estimation calculation "
"and saves the results for later evaluation using the B<rateest> match."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-name> I<name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Count matched packets into the pool referred to by I<name>, which is freely "
"choosable."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-interval> I<amount>{B<s>|B<ms>|B<us>}"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Rate measurement interval, in seconds, milliseconds or microseconds."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--rateest-ewmalog> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Rate measurement averaging time constant."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "REDIRECT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is only valid in the B<nat> table, in the B<PREROUTING> and "
"B<OUTPUT> chains, and user-defined chains which are only called from those "
"chains.  It redirects the packet to the machine itself by changing the "
"destination IP to the primary address of the incoming interface (locally-"
"generated packets are mapped to the localhost address, 127.0.0.1 for IPv4 "
"and ::1 for IPv6, and packets arriving on interfaces that don't have an IP "
"address configured are dropped)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This specifies a destination port or range of ports to use: without this, "
"the destination port is never altered.  This is only valid if the rule also "
"specifies one of the following protocols: B<tcp>, B<udp>, B<dccp> or "
"B<sctp>.  For a single port, a service name as listed in B</etc/services> "
"may be used."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "IPv6 support available starting Linux kernels E<gt>= 3.7."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "REJECT (IPv6-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is used to send back an error packet in response to the matched packet: "
"otherwise it is equivalent to B<DROP> so it is a terminating TARGET, ending "
"rule traversal.  This target is only valid in the B<INPUT>, B<FORWARD> and "
"B<OUTPUT> chains, and user-defined chains which are only called from those "
"chains.  The following option controls the nature of the error packet "
"returned:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--reject-with> I<type>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The type given can be B<icmp6-no-route>, B<no-route>, B<icmp6-adm-"
"prohibited>, B<adm-prohibited>, B<icmp6-addr-unreachable>, B<addr-unreach>, "
"or B<icmp6-port-unreachable>, which return the appropriate ICMPv6 error "
"message (B<icmp6-port-unreachable> is the default). Finally, the option "
"B<tcp-reset> can be used on rules which only match the TCP protocol: this "
"causes a TCP RST packet to be sent back.  This is mainly useful for blocking "
"I<ident> (113/tcp) probes which frequently occur when sending mail to broken "
"mail hosts (which won't accept your mail otherwise).  B<tcp-reset> can only "
"be used with kernel versions 2.6.14 or later."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"I<Warning:> You should not indiscriminately apply the REJECT target to "
"packets whose connection state is classified as INVALID; instead, you should "
"only DROP these."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Consider a source host transmitting a packet P, with P experiencing so much "
"delay along its path that the source host issues a retransmission, P_2, with "
"P_2 being successful in reaching its destination and advancing the "
"connection state normally. It is conceivable that the late-arriving P may be "
"considered not to be associated with any connection tracking entry. "
"Generating a reject response for a packet so classed would then terminate "
"the healthy connection."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "So, instead of:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-A INPUT ... -j REJECT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "do consider using:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"-A INPUT ... -m conntrack --ctstate INVALID -j DROP -A INPUT ... -j REJECT"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "REJECT (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The type given can be B<icmp-net-unreachable>, B<icmp-host-unreachable>, "
"B<icmp-port-unreachable>, B<icmp-proto-unreachable>, B<icmp-net-prohibited>, "
"B<icmp-host-prohibited>, or B<icmp-admin-prohibited> (*), which return the "
"appropriate ICMP error message (B<icmp-port-unreachable> is the default).  "
"The option B<tcp-reset> can be used on rules which only match the TCP "
"protocol: this causes a TCP RST packet to be sent back.  This is mainly "
"useful for blocking I<ident> (113/tcp) probes which frequently occur when "
"sending mail to broken mail hosts (which won't accept your mail otherwise)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"(*) Using icmp-admin-prohibited with kernels that do not support it will "
"result in a plain DROP instead of REJECT"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "SECMARK"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is used to set the security mark value associated with the packet for "
"use by security subsystems such as SELinux.  It is valid in the B<security> "
"table (for backwards compatibility with older kernels, it is also valid in "
"the B<mangle> table). The mark is 32 bits wide."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--selctx> I<security_context>"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "SET"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module adds and/or deletes entries from IP sets which can be defined by "
"ipset(8)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--add-set> I<setname> I<flag>[B<,>I<flag>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "add the address(es)/port(s) of the packet to the set"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--del-set> I<setname> I<flag>[B<,>I<flag>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "delete the address(es)/port(s) of the packet from the set"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--map-set> I<setname> I<flag>[B<,>I<flag>...] "
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"[--map-mark] [--map-prio] [--map-queue] map packet properties (firewall "
"mark, tc priority, hardware queue)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"where I<flag>(s) are B<src> and/or B<dst> specifications and there can be no "
"more than six of them."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--timeout> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"when adding an entry, the timeout value to use instead of the default one "
"from the set definition"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--exist>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"when adding an entry if it already exists, reset the timeout value to the "
"specified one or to the default from the set definition"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--map-set> I<set-name>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"the set-name should be created with --skbinfo option B<--map-mark> map "
"firewall mark to packet by lookup of value in the set B<--map-prio> map "
"traffic control priority to packet by lookup of value in the set B<--map-"
"queue> map hardware NIC queue to packet by lookup of value in the set"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<--map-set> option can be used from the mangle table only. The B<--map-"
"prio> and B<--map-queue> flags can be used in the OUTPUT, FORWARD and "
"POSTROUTING chains."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Use of -j SET requires that ipset kernel support is provided, which, for "
"standard kernels, is the case since Linux 2.6.39."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "SNAT"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is only valid in the B<nat> table, in the B<POSTROUTING> and "
"B<INPUT> chains, and user-defined chains which are only called from those "
"chains.  It specifies that the source address of the packet should be "
"modified (and all future packets in this connection will also be mangled), "
"and rules should cease being examined.  It takes the following options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--to-source> [I<ipaddr>[B<->I<ipaddr>]][B<:>I<port>[B<->I<port>]]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"which can specify a single new source IP address, an inclusive range of IP "
"addresses. Optionally a port range, if the rule also specifies one of the "
"following protocols: B<tcp>, B<udp>, B<dccp> or B<sctp>.  If no port range "
"is specified, then source ports below 512 will be mapped to other ports "
"below 512: those between 512 and 1023 inclusive will be mapped to ports "
"below 1024, and other ports will be mapped to 1024 or above. Where possible, "
"no port alteration will occur."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Randomize source port mapping through a hash-based algorithm (kernel E<gt>= "
"2.6.21)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Fully randomize source port mapping through a PRNG (kernel E<gt>= 3.14)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Kernels prior to 2.6.36-rc1 don't have the ability to B<SNAT> in the "
"B<INPUT> chain."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "SNPT (IPv6-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Provides stateless source IPv6-to-IPv6 Network Prefix Translation (as "
"described by RFC 6296)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "You have to use the DNPT target to undo the translation. Example:"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "SYNPROXY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target will process TCP three-way-handshake parallel in netfilter "
"context to protect either local or backend system. This target requires "
"connection tracking because sequence numbers need to be translated.  The "
"kernels ability to absorb SYNFLOOD was greatly improved starting with Linux "
"4.4, so this target should not be needed anymore to protect Linux servers."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--mss> I<maximum segment size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Maximum segment size announced to clients. This must match the backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--wscale> I<window scale>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Window scale announced to clients. This must match the backend."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--sack-perm>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Pass client selective acknowledgement option to backend (will be disabled if "
"not present)."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--timestamps>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Pass client timestamp option to backend (will be disabled if not present, "
"also needed for selective acknowledgement and window scaling)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Determine tcp options used by backend, from an external system"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "tcpdump -pni eth0 -c 1 'tcp[tcpflags] == (tcp-syn|tcp-ack)'"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    port 80 &\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "telnet 192.0.2.42 80"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "18:57:24.693307 IP 192.0.2.42.80 E<gt> 192.0.2.43.48757:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    Flags [S.], seq 360414582, ack 788841994, win 14480,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    options [mss 1460,sackOK,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    TS val 1409056151 ecr 9690221,\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    nop,wscale 9],\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "    length 0\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Switch tcp_loose mode off, so conntrack will mark out-of-flow packets as "
"state INVALID."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Make SYN packets untracked"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"iptables -t raw -A PREROUTING -i eth0 -p tcp --dport 80\n"
"    --syn -j CT --notrack\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Catch UNTRACKED (SYN packets) and INVALID (3WHS ACK packets) states and send "
"them to SYNPROXY. This rule will respond to SYN packets with SYN+ACK "
"syncookies, create ESTABLISHED for valid client response (3WHS ACK packets) "
"and drop incorrect cookies. Flags combinations not expected during 3WHS will "
"not match and continue (e.g. SYN+FIN, SYN+ACK)."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"iptables -A INPUT -i eth0 -p tcp --dport 80\n"
"    -m state --state UNTRACKED,INVALID -j SYNPROXY\n"
"    --sack-perm --timestamp --mss 1460 --wscale 9\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Drop invalid packets, this will be out-of-flow packets that were not matched "
"by SYNPROXY."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"iptables -A INPUT -i eth0 -p tcp --dport 80 -m state --state INVALID -j DROP"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TCPMSS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target alters the MSS value of TCP SYN packets, to control the maximum "
"size for that connection (usually limiting it to your outgoing interface's "
"MTU minus 40 for IPv4 or 60 for IPv6, respectively).  Of course, it can only "
"be used in conjunction with B<-p tcp>."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is used to overcome criminally braindead ISPs or servers which "
"block \"ICMP Fragmentation Needed\" or \"ICMPv6 Packet Too Big\" packets.  "
"The symptoms of this problem are that everything works fine from your Linux "
"firewall/router, but machines behind it can never exchange large packets:"
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "1."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Web browsers connect, then hang with no data received."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "2."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Small mail works fine, but large emails hang."
msgstr ""

#. type: IP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "3."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "ssh works fine, but scp hangs after initial handshaking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Workaround: activate this option and add a rule to your firewall "
"configuration like:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
" iptables -t mangle -A FORWARD -p tcp --tcp-flags SYN,RST SYN\n"
"             -j TCPMSS --clamp-mss-to-pmtu\n"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-mss> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Explicitly sets MSS option to specified value. If the MSS of the packet is "
"already lower than I<value>, it will B<not> be increased (from Linux 2.6.25 "
"onwards) to avoid more problems with hosts relying on a proper MSS."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--clamp-mss-to-pmtu>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Automatically clamp MSS value to (path_MTU - 40 for IPv4; -60 for IPv6).  "
"This may not function as desired where asymmetric routes with differing path "
"MTU exist \\(em the kernel uses the path MTU which it would use to send "
"packets from itself to the source and destination IP addresses. Prior to "
"Linux 2.6.25, only the path MTU to the destination IP address was considered "
"by this option; subsequent kernels also consider the path MTU to the source "
"IP address."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "These options are mutually exclusive."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TCPOPTSTRIP"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target will strip TCP options off a TCP packet. (It will actually "
"replace them by NO-OPs.) As such, you will need to add the B<-p tcp> "
"parameters."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--strip-options> I<option>[B<,>I<option>...]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Strip the given option(s). The options may be specified by TCP option number "
"or by symbolic name. The list of recognized options can be obtained by "
"calling iptables with B<-j TCPOPTSTRIP -h>."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TEE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"The B<TEE> target will clone a packet and redirect this clone to another "
"machine on the B<local> network segment. In other words, the nexthop must be "
"the target, or you will have to configure the nexthop to forward it further "
"if so desired."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--gateway> I<ipaddr>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Send the cloned packet to the host reachable at the given IP address.  Use "
"of 0.0.0.0 (for IPv4 packets) or :: (IPv6) is invalid."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"To forward all incoming traffic on eth0 to an Network Layer logging box:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "-t mangle -A PREROUTING -i eth0 -j TEE --gateway 2001:db8::1"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TOS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This module sets the Type of Service field in the IPv4 header (including the "
"\"precedence\" bits) or the Priority field in the IPv6 header. Note that TOS "
"shares the same bits as DSCP and ECN. The TOS target is only valid in the "
"B<mangle> table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-tos> I<value>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Zeroes out the bits given by I<mask> (see NOTE below) and XORs I<value> into "
"the TOS/Priority field. If I<mask> is omitted, 0xFF is assumed."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--set-tos> I<symbol>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"You can specify a symbolic name when using the TOS target for IPv4. It "
"implies a mask of 0xFF (see NOTE below). The list of recognized TOS names "
"can be obtained by calling iptables with B<-j TOS -h>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--and-tos> I<bits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary AND the TOS value with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-tos 0/"
">I<invbits>, where I<invbits> is the binary negation of I<bits>.  See NOTE "
"below.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--or-tos> I<bits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary OR the TOS value with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-tos> I<bits>B</"
">I<bits>. See NOTE below.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--xor-tos> I<bits>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Binary XOR the TOS value with I<bits>. (Mnemonic for B<--set-tos> I<bits>B</"
"0>. See NOTE below.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"NOTE: In Linux kernels up to and including 2.6.38, with the exception of "
"longterm releases 2.6.32 (E<gt>=.42), 2.6.33 (E<gt>=.15), and 2.6.35 "
"(E<gt>=.14), there is a bug whereby IPv6 TOS mangling does not behave as "
"documented and differs from the IPv4 version. The TOS mask indicates the "
"bits one wants to zero out, so it needs to be inverted before applying it to "
"the original TOS field. However, the aformentioned kernels forgo the "
"inversion which breaks --set-tos and its mnemonics."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TPROXY"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target is only valid in the B<mangle> table, in the B<PREROUTING> chain "
"and user-defined chains which are only called from this chain. It redirects "
"the packet to a local socket without changing the packet header in any way. "
"It can also change the mark value which can then be used in advanced routing "
"rules.  It takes three options:"
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--on-port> I<port>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This specifies a destination port to use. It is a required option, 0 means "
"the new destination port is the same as the original. This is only valid if "
"the rule also specifies B<-p tcp> or B<-p udp>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--on-ip> I<address>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This specifies a destination address to use. By default the address is the "
"IP address of the incoming interface. This is only valid if the rule also "
"specifies B<-p tcp> or B<-p udp>."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--tproxy-mark> I<value>[B</>I<mask>]"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Marks packets with the given value/mask. The fwmark value set here can be "
"used by advanced routing. (Required for transparent proxying to work: "
"otherwise these packets will get forwarded, which is probably not what you "
"want.)"
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TRACE"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This target marks packets so that the kernel will log every rule which match "
"the packets as those traverse the tables, chains, rules. It can only be used "
"in the B<raw> table."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"With iptables-legacy, a logging backend, such as ip(6)t_LOG or "
"nfnetlink_log, must be loaded for this to be visible.  The packets are "
"logged with the string prefix: \"TRACE: tablename:chainname:type:rulenum \" "
"where type can be \"rule\" for plain rule, \"return\" for implicit rule at "
"the end of a user defined chain and \"policy\" for the policy of the built "
"in chains."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"With iptables-nft, the target is translated into nftables' B<meta nftrace> "
"expression. Hence the kernel sends trace events via netlink to userspace "
"where they may be displayed using B<xtables-monitor --trace> command. For "
"details, refer to B<xtables-monitor>(8)."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "TTL (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"This is used to modify the IPv4 TTL header field.  The TTL field determines "
"how many hops (routers) a packet can traverse until it's time to live is "
"exceeded."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Setting or incrementing the TTL field can potentially be very dangerous, so "
"it should be avoided at any cost. This target is only valid in B<mangle> "
"table."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ttl-set> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Set the TTL value to `value'."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ttl-dec> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Decrement the TTL value `value' times."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ttl-inc> I<value>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid "Increment the TTL value `value' times."
msgstr ""

#. type: SS
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "ULOG (IPv4-specific)"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"This is the deprecated ipv4-only predecessor of the NFLOG target.  It "
"provides userspace logging of matching packets.  When this target is set for "
"a rule, the Linux kernel will multicast this packet through a I<netlink> "
"socket. One or more userspace processes may then subscribe to various "
"multicast groups and receive the packets.  Like LOG, this is a \"non-"
"terminating target\", i.e. rule traversal continues at the next rule."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ulog-nlgroup> I<nlgroup>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm opensuse-leap-16-0
msgid ""
"This specifies the netlink group (1-32) to which the packet is sent.  "
"Default value is 1."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ulog-prefix> I<prefix>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Prefix log messages with the specified prefix; up to 32 characters long, and "
"useful for distinguishing messages in the logs."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ulog-cprange> I<size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Number of bytes to be copied to userspace.  A value of 0 always copies the "
"entire packet, regardless of its size.  Default is 0."
msgstr ""

#. type: TP
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
#, no-wrap
msgid "B<--ulog-qthreshold> I<size>"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: archlinux debian-bookworm debian-unstable mageia-cauldron opensuse-leap-16-0
#: opensuse-tumbleweed
msgid ""
"Number of packet to queue inside kernel.  Setting this value to, e.g. 10 "
"accumulates ten packets inside the kernel and transmits them as one netlink "
"multipart message to userspace.  Default is 1 (for backwards compatibility)."
msgstr ""

